+findings:
+  - id: ESD-03-DF-01
+    found_by: "ESD-03"
+    found_at_commit: "3e57ea9e"
+    schedule_revision: 1
+    severity: major
+    blocking: false
+    channel: independent-review
+    area: "test_graph node spec.workflow.cleanup: delete path from an absent context value"
+    surface:
+      production: []
+      tla: []
+      adapters: []
+      test_graph: ["test_graph/sources/spec_workflow_cleanup.py"]
+      workflow: []
+    summary: >-
+      spec.workflow.cleanup deletes `Path(ctx.get("spec.workflow.repo", "repoPath") or "")`.
+      With no published repoPath, that path is `Path("")` == `.`. A uv node's working directory is
+      the test_graph project directory (UvExecutor sets `.directory(invocation.projectDir)`), so
+      `shutil.rmtree(".")` deletes test_graph/ itself. The node is a finalizer: it runs after an
+      upstream failure once spec.workflow.repo has executed, even if that node errored without
+      publishing. Under --continue-after-failure it runs unconditionally. This is the shape of the
+      recorded incident "a failing graph node deleted 27 tracked files of test_graph/ itself"
+      (specs/results/epic-self-improvement-substrate/review/wave-3/review.md, item 3). The fix
+      recorded there changed the install path (tla_spec_dev_cli_install.py comment). The delete
+      guard is still absent at 3e57ea9e. Not reproduced here: reproducing it would delete the
+      checkout's test_graph/.
+    reproduction: "Read test_graph/sources/spec_workflow_cleanup.py main(); python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; print(Path(\"\") == Path(\".\"))' prints True."
+    evidence:
+      - "test_graph/sources/spec_workflow_cleanup.py"
+      - "skills/test-graph/project_sdk_sources/build-logic/src/main/kotlin/com/hayden/testgraphsdk/exec/PlanExecutor.kt (shouldRunAfterFailure)"
+      - "skills/test-graph/references/graph-architecture-review.md (rule E2, worked review)"
+    why_out_of_scope: >-
+      test_graph/sources/ is not in ESD-03's conflict keys, and the assignment forbids code changes
+      in this instruction-only ticket.
+    suggested_fix: >-
+      Delete only when repoPath is non-empty and resolves under ctx.report_dir. Assert that as a
+      named assertion, so a refusal is a red with the path, not silent residue. Keep rerun(False).
+    skill_change: none
+    blast_radius: "Destructive: the project's own validation sources; every graph that composes the cleanup node (specWorkflow, the probe's nested graph)."
+    disposition: pending
+    disposition_ticket: null
+
+  - id: ESD-03-DF-02
+    found_by: "ESD-03"
+    found_at_commit: "3e57ea9e"
+    schedule_revision: 1
+    severity: minor
+    blocking: false
+    channel: independent-review
+    area: "test_graph node spec.workflow.failure_cleanup_probe: contract (kind, dependsOn, sideEffects, budget)"
+    surface:
+      production: []
+      tla: []
+      adapters: []
+      test_graph: ["test_graph/sources/spec_workflow_failure_cleanup_probe.py", "test_graph/build.gradle.kts"]
+      workflow: []
+    summary: >-
+      The node behind ESD-01 rows RP-07-DF-01 and BS-07-DF-05 is an `assertion` that copies a Test
+      Graph project and runs a nested Gradle build. It declares only `fs:tmp`, although the
+      registered `process:gradle` exists for exactly this. It depends on spec.workflow.close but
+      reads only spec.workflow.repo's sourceRepo. It is tagged `finalizer`, so it runs after an
+      upstream failure. Its fixed 180 s timeout bounds a cold build-logic compile plus a 20 s drain.
+      In specWorkflow it is listed before spec.reference.adapters_resolve, which was skipped behind
+      it in bug-sweep milestone 1.
+    reproduction: "Read the NodeSpec in test_graph/sources/spec_workflow_failure_cleanup_probe.py and the specWorkflow block in test_graph/build.gradle.kts."
+    evidence:
+      - "specs/results/evidence-sized-delivery/ESD-01/inventory.yaml (rows RP-07-DF-01, BS-07-DF-05)"
+      - "skills/test-graph/references/graph-architecture-review.md (rules A1, A3, A4, D2; worked review)"
+    why_out_of_scope: "Node source and graph definition are outside ESD-03's conflict keys; instruction-only ticket."
+    suggested_fix: >-
+      Split the project copy into a fixture node. Declare process:gradle. Depend on spec.workflow.repo
+      only. Size the timeout from a recorded cold run. Place adapters_resolve so that it does not
+      share fate with the probe. Show the probe red on a planted residue before trusting it again.
+    skill_change: none
+    blast_radius: "specWorkflow only; changes node metadata and order, not node ids."
+    disposition: pending
+    disposition_ticket: null
+
+  - id: ESD-03-DF-03
+    found_by: "ESD-03"
+    found_at_commit: "3e57ea9e"
+    schedule_revision: 1
